<http://data.silknow.org/object/884f3069-acab-3f7d-adf5-ab79e2d64094/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "woven silk backed with cotton twill and faced with woven silk.\nPart of a woven silk shawl of the 'Husein Quli Khan' type with an integral border on three sides; cut across the bottom. The ground is dark blue and a slightly diagonal right facing boteh is repeated 12 times per row. Straight repeat. A pair of green leaves form the bottom of the boteh and then small segments form an internal band around a spray of small flower heads.  There is a round blossom enclosed by the curving tip of the boteh. The colours are: green, light green, orange, white.\nThe narrow border contains a geometric meander with a 6-petalled flower with an orange centre.\nBacking: pieced red cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut striped silk; dark blue and white stripes each containing an isolated motif."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/884f3069-acab-3f7d-adf5-ab79e2d64094> .

