<http://data.silknow.org/object/884f3069-acab-3f7d-adf5-ab79e2d64094>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "woven silk backed with cotton twill and faced with woven silk.\nPart of a woven silk shawl of the 'Husein Quli Khan' type with an integral border on three sides; cut across the bottom. The ground is dark blue and a slightly diagonal right facing boteh is repeated 12 times per row. Straight repeat. A pair of green leaves form the bottom of the boteh and then small segments form an internal band around a spray of small flower heads.  There is a round blossom enclosed by the curving tip of the boteh. The colours are: green, light green, orange, white.\nThe narrow border contains a geometric meander with a 6-petalled flower with an orange centre.\nBacking: pieced red cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut striped silk; dark blue and white stripes each containing an isolated motif."@en , "Middle East, Textile;"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/468076ef-0d40-3289-a40b-d819b49e0190> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/30128f6b-dc0e-31cd-b4d2-6cccab617111> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/67a4e371-851a-32c9-83bb-b2e5d47650e3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ab1167f5-065b-37c7-bc0b-8ed802401f6a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "woven silk backed with cotton twill and faced with woven silk.\nPart of a woven silk shawl of the 'Husein Quli Khan' type with an integral border on three sides; cut across the bottom. The ground is dark blue and a slightly diagonal right facing boteh is repeated 12 times per row. Straight repeat. A pair of green leaves form the bottom of the boteh and then small segments form an internal band around a spray of small flower heads.  There is a round blossom enclosed by the curving tip of the boteh. The colours are: green, light green, orange, white.\nThe narrow border contains a geometric meander with a 6-petalled flower with an orange centre.\nBacking: pieced red cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut striped silk; dark blue and white stripes each containing an isolated motif."@en , "Middle East, Textile;"@en ;
